INT. ST. CLEMENT'S HOSPITAL, TRAUMA BAY THREE - NIGHT

Overhead lights. Monitors beep. A body on a gurney under blue drapes.

DR. ANWEN OKOYE-FITZGERALD (40s, surgeon, scrubs, mask pulled down) works at the bedside. Beside her, NURSE TADEUSZ MBEKI-LORENZ (30s, calm, gloved) hands her a clamp. At the foot of the gurney, RESIDENT DR. PRIYANKA HALVORSEN-NWOSU (20s, new, eyes huge) watches, clipboard clutched.

On the wall, a speaker crackles.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Trauma Three, ETA on the second unit, four minutes.

ANWEN
Copy. We're stable.

TADEUSZ
Pressure's dropping.

ANWEN
Fluids?

TADEUSZ
Wide open.

ANWEN
Priyanka, what's your call?

PRIYANKA
Um. Blood?

ANWEN
Correct. Type?

PRIYANKA
O negative. Universal.

ANWEN
Go get four units.

PRIYANKA
Right now?

ANWEN
Yesterday.

Priyanka bolts through the door. Tadeusz watches her go.

TADEUSZ
She'll be fine.

ANWEN
They all say that.

TADEUSZ
She will be.

ANWEN
Pressure.

TADEUSZ
Eighty over fifty.

ANWEN
Pulse?

TADEUSZ
One-thirty.

ANWEN
Pack it. Pack it, pack it.

He packs. She presses. The monitor rises, falters, steadies.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Trauma Three, update. Second unit is reporting a child on board. Pediatric trauma, eight years old.

Anwen and Tadeusz exchange a look.

ANWEN
Open Bay Four.

TADEUSZ
Dr. Okoye-Fitzgerald, we're short.

ANWEN
Then call Reyes in from the cafeteria.

TADEUSZ
She's off.

ANWEN
Call her anyway.

He is already dialing. The door bursts open. Priyanka, breathless, carries a cooler of blood bags.

PRIYANKA
Four units, O negative.

ANWEN
Good. Hang two. Then you're with me in Four.

PRIYANKA
The child?

ANWEN
The child.

Priyanka stares. Then she sets down the cooler, rolls up her sleeves, and nods once.

ANWEN (CONT'D)
(softly)
You'll be fine.

PRIYANKA
They all say that.

Anwen almost smiles. Pulls up her mask. Out the door.
